target:    .github/workflows/ci.yml
gate:      composer test:perf-gate-integrity
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    does not carry always()
rationale: Removes always() from the EXPLAIN gate, returning it to a step that has never executed once in the history of this pipeline. It sits after k6, and k6 failed on every dispatch this lane ever had. Section 3 pins the gate's CONTENTS -- it must exist, must not be a TODO, must carry no `exit 0`, must invoke explain-gate.sh -- and every one of those assertions was true and working the whole time. They answer 'could this gate fail?'; nothing answered 'did it run?'. PITFALLS 111.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@
       # those are two different claims. A gate proven capable of failing, in a
       # lane that never reaches it, is the recurring shape one altitude up.
       - name: EXPLAIN gate — full-table-scan check
-        if: ${{ matrix.php == '8.2' && always() }}
+        if: ${{ matrix.php == '8.2' }}
         env:
           EXPLAIN_ROW_THRESHOLD: "100000"
         run: bash tests/perf/explain-gate.sh
